  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expected Results</narrative>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">R&#xe9;sultats escompt&#xe9;s</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results expected</narrative>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">R&#xe9;sultats escompt&#xe9;s</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expected results include: (1) increased access by Canadian interns to Canadian labour market opportunities, including in the field of international development; and (2) increased engagement of Canadian interns as global citizens in supporting international development efforts in Canada and abroad.</narrative>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Les r&#xe9;sultats interm&#xe9;diaires escompt&#xe9;s de ce projet comprennent : 1) les stagiaires Autochtones (femmes et hommes) sont activement &#xe0; la recherche de possibilit&#xe9;s d&#x2019;emploi ou d&#x2019;&#xe9;tudes au Canada, y compris dans des domaines li&#xe9;s au d&#xe9;veloppement international; 2) les stagiaires Autochtones (femmes et hommes), en tant que citoyens du monde, participent au soutien des efforts en mati&#xe8;re de d&#xe9;veloppement international au Canada et &#xe0; l&#x2019;&#xe9;tranger.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results achieved</narrative>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">R&#xe9;sultats atteints</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results achieved</narrative>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">R&#xe9;sultats atteints</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Parmi les r&#xe9;sultats obtenus jusqu&apos;en mars 2017 : 1) 15 stagiaires (7 femmes et 8 hommes) ont &#xe9;t&#xe9; recrut&#xe9;s et d&#xe9;ploy&#xe9;s, quatre au S&#xe9;n&#xe9;gal et onze en &#xc9;quateur; 2) les 15 stagiaires affirment avoir bien &#xe9;t&#xe9; form&#xe9;s sur les enjeux li&#xe9;s au d&#xe9;veloppement y compris la viabilit&#xe9; environnementale, la gouvernance et l&apos;&#xe9;galit&#xe9; entre les sexes; 3) 73 % des  stagiaires  affirment que les comp&#xe9;tences acquises durant le stage favoriseront leur entr&#xe9;e sur le march&#xe9; du travail.</narrative>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results achieved as of March 2017 include: (1) 15 interns (7 female and 8 male) were recruited and sent abroad, four to Senegal and 11 to Ecuador; (2) the 15 interns stated that they were well trained on development-related issues, including environmental sustainability, governance and gender equality; and (3) 73 % of the interns stated that the skills acquired during the placement would help them enter the labour market.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
  </result>
